body.input:
First call the getBoard operation of the plant_maintenance_system tool (a direct tool call - it is not available in Code Interpreter) to read the open work orders and quality holds. Then write the handover for @{triggerBody()?['line']}, @{triggerBody()?['shift']} shift of @{triggerBody()?['date']} and add a section 'Incident @{workflow()?['run']?['name']}' that summarises what was done:
- Quality triage: @{outputs('Triage_fields')?['summary']} Root cause: @{outputs('Triage_fields')?['root_cause']} Quality holds: @{variables('holds')}
- Maintenance diagnosis: @{variables('diagnosis')}
- Visual inspection: @{variables('inspection')}
- Work order: @{variables('workOrder')}
In 'Open work orders & quality holds', list the records returned by getBoard. Keep the whole handover under 400 words.
